---
import Reference from '../layouts/Reference.astro';
import { loadDocs } from '../lib/content';
import { buildSourceRegister } from '../lib/sourceRegister';
const sources = buildSourceRegister(await loadDocs());
---

<Reference
  title="Further reading"
  description="Explore the reading behind HELM and simple tips for applying the guidance to your team."
>
  <h1>Further reading</h1>
  <p>
    HELM brings together practical advice for working with AI agents. Start with
    the <a href="/foundation">six principles</a> and try the guides on your own
    work. The reading below offers more detail when you need it.
  </p>
  <p>
    The guides suggest ways to work; they do not guarantee results. Examples and
    planning targets are there to help you get started. Check what works for
    your team and adjust as you learn.
  </p>
  <h2 id="sources">Explore the reading</h2>
  <p>
    These articles include practical advice, surveys, and authors’ experiences.
    They offer different perspectives, rather than proof of the whole framework.
  </p>
  <ul>
    {sources.map((source) => (
      <li id={source.id}>
        <a href={source.url}>{source.title.replaceAll('_', '')}</a>
      </li>
    ))}
  </ul>
  <h2 id="claims">Applying what you read</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Try one practice on a small piece of work before using it more widely.
    </li>
    <li>Treat team sizes, dates, and targets as examples to adapt.</li>
    <li>Look at quality and review effort alongside speed.</li>
    <li>
      Use the role guides to discuss learning, rather than to score people.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    The <a href="/practitioners">Practitioner Guide</a> helps you plan and check
    the work. The <a href="/leadership">Leadership Guide</a> helps you discuss
    responsibilities and learning with your team.
  </p>
  <h2 id="maintenance">Help improve HELM</h2>
  <p>
    Found something unclear or incorrect?{' '}
    <a href="https://github.com/firaskafri/helm-framework.com/issues/new">
      Tell us which page you were reading and what would help.
    </a>
  </p>
</Reference>
